- Input: A CSV or Excel file containing Account Name, DB Name, Priv. Type, Obj. Type, and Object Name.
- Processing: Groups permissions into an account/database/privilege/object hierarchy, then creates summaries by account and privilege type, and by database and object type.
- Output: An .xlsx workbook with three sheets: Detailed_Hierarchy, Account_Priv_Summary, and DB_Object_Summary.
- Interface and packaging: A Tkinter GUI handles file selection and displays status; the .spec file and dist\UserRightScan.exe indicate it’s packaged as a standalone Windows executable. The notebook contains an earlier version and a copy of the current script.
